PART 2 — INDEPENDENT GRAMMAR CORRECTION SETTINGS

THIS IS A REQUIRED CORE FEATURE.

Create a clearly labeled setting:

Corrections During Conversation

This setting must be available in both Friendly Conversation Partner and Structured Language Tutor.

Do not make grammar correction behavior permanently dependent on the selected AI personality.

The learner must be able to customize their preferred learning experience.

Correction options

OFF — REVIEW AFTER CONVERSATION

No unsolicited grammar corrections during the spoken conversation.

The AI continues naturally.

Grammar mistakes can still be analyzed and collected for an end-of-session review, if the learner has enabled review analysis.

The learner may manually request:

* Correct My Last Sentence.
* Explain My Grammar.
* Show a More Natural Version.

Do not automatically announce errors during conversation.

Do not display distracting correction notifications.

Do not silently discard grammar-learning opportunities if post-session review is enabled.

DISCREET — SUBTLE CORRECTIONS

This is the default for Friendly Conversation Partner.

The AI continues speaking naturally.

When a meaningful error is detected:

* Display a small, unobtrusive correction indicator beside the relevant transcript message.
* Do not interrupt spoken dialogue.
* Do not automatically read grammar explanations aloud.
* Let the learner open a correction card when interested.
* Preserve conversation flow.

The learner can view the correction immediately or ignore it until the session ends.

Example:

Learner:

“Я живу в Львів.”

AI:

“О, ти живеш у Львові! А як давно ти там живеш?”

The transcript may display a small grammar indicator beside the learner’s message.

Tapping it opens:

Original: Я живу в Львів.

Correct: Я живу у Львові.

Explanation: The locative form Львові is used when expressing location with у/в.

GENTLE — IMPORTANT CORRECTIONS ONLY

Correct errors that significantly affect meaning or reflect important recurring mistakes.

Keep feedback short.

Allow the learner to continue speaking without lengthy interruptions.

BALANCED — ACTIVE LEARNING

This is the default for Structured Language Tutor.

Correct significant grammar mistakes, unnatural constructions, and important vocabulary errors.

Explain corrections clearly and briefly.

Offer a retry opportunity when it would improve learning.

Do not correct every minor stylistic difference.

INTENSIVE — DETAILED CORRECTION

Provide comprehensive feedback on most meaningful grammar errors.

Include:

* Corrected sentence.
* Grammar explanation.
* Relevant case or conjugation pattern.
* Natural alternatives.
* Retry opportunity.
* Additional examples when appropriate.

Even in Intensive mode, avoid interrupting mid-sentence.

Provide corrections between completed conversational turns.

Do not turn every response into an excessively long lecture.

